BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discussion: The President of the Church [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTSTAMP:20260921T203200Z
UID:event-assignment-1441108
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/p
 review?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 40 minutes\n\nWatch this video about d
 iscussion board guidelines for the semester:\n\n[Discussions Transcript] (
 https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505320?wrap=1)\n\nYou wi
 ll have the opportunity in upcoming lessons to study many talks and messag
 es taught by President Oaks. In this unit\, you have learned more about hi
 s calling and his biography. Now we will consider this question together: 
 In what ways is his life a sermon? Follow the prompts below to share lesso
 ns you learned from his life experience.\n\nFor this discussion\, you will
  make two separate posts:\n\n* Post 1\, due by Tuesday: Write two solid pa
 ragraphs (4–6 sentences each)\n\n* Each paragraph should very briefly me
 ntion one particular life theme or event from President Oaks's life (you d
 o not need to repeat its details)\,\n\n* Then explain what principles you 
 learned\, and\n\n* Comment on how you can apply that example in your own l
 ife and circumstances.\n\n* Post 2\, due by Wednesday: After reading 5+ of
  your peers' posts\, make a separate\, one-paragraph Summary + Response po
 st. What themes and additional ideas stood out to you in the examples and 
 thoughts they shared?\n\nFull points will be rewarded for one initial post
  plus a later Summary + Response post\, with each demonstrating considered
  engagement related to the lesson material.\n\nRubric: You will earn up to
  6 points for the content and requirements of your initial post (each para
 graph: event\, principle\, application) and 4 points for your thoughtful s
 ummary and response to the group discussion. To see the complete rubric\, 
 click on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click "
 Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item Completion (built in browser\, hidden in app)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=09&year=2026#assignment_1441108
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instruct
 ure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409020
 /dp_app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructure-uploads.s3.a
 mazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8073295/canvas-byuonlin
 e-app.css"><p><img src="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13
 505106/preview?hidden=1" alt="" width="2389" height="554" data-decorative=
 "true" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044
 /files/13505106" data-api-returntype="File" loading="lazy"></p>\n<p><span 
 style="font-size: 10pt\;"><em>Estimated time: 40 minutes</em></span></p>\n
 <p><strong>Watch this video about discussion board guidelines for the seme
 ster:</strong></p>\n<p><iframe style="border: 1px solid #464646\;" title="
 Discussion guidelines" src="https://byu.hosted.panopto.com/Panopto/Pages/E
 mbed.aspx?id=33c46812-5504-4114-b881-aed20162ac35&amp\;autoplay=false&amp
 \;offerviewer=true&amp\;showtitle=true&amp\;showbrand=false&amp\;start=0&a
 mp\;interactivity=all" width="720" height="405" loading="lazy" allowfullsc
 reen="allowfullscreen" allow="autoplay"></iframe></p>\n<p><span style="fon
 t-size: 8pt\;"><a id="5262342" class="instructure_file_link instructure_sc
 ribd_file inline_disabled" href="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044
 /files/13505320?wrap=1" target="_blank" data-canvas-previewable="true" dat
 a-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044/files/135
 05320" data-api-returntype="File">Discussions Transcript</a></span></p>\n<
 p><span style="color: #000000\;">You will have the opportunity in upcoming
  lessons to study many talks and messages taught by President Oaks. In thi
 s unit\, you have learned more about his calling and his biography. Now we
  will consider this question together: <em>In what ways is his life a serm
 on?</em> Follow the prompts below to share lessons you learned from his li
 fe experience.</span></p>\n<p><span style="color: #000000\;">For this disc
 ussion\, you will make two separate posts:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>P
 ost 1\, </strong>due by Tuesday: Write <span style="text-decoration: under
 line\;">two</span> solid paragraphs (4–6 sentences each)\n<ul>\n<li><spa
 n style="color: #000000\;">Each paragraph should very briefly mention one 
 particular life theme or event from President Oaks's life (you do not need
  to repeat its details)\,</span></li>\n<li><span style="color: #000000\;">
 Then explain what principles you learned\, and </span></li>\n<li><span sty
 le="color: #000000\;">Comment on how <em>you</em> can apply that example i
 n your own life and circumstances.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><span st
 yle="color: #000000\;"><strong>Post 2\, </strong>due by Wednesday: After r
 eading 5+ of your peers' posts\, make a separate\, one-paragraph <em>Summa
 ry + Response</em> post. What themes and additional ideas stood out to you
  in the examples and thoughts they shared?</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span st
 yle="color: #000000\;">Full points will be rewarded for one initial post p
 lus a later <em>Summary + Response</em> post\, with each demonstrating con
 sidered engagement related to the lesson material.</span></p>\n<p><span st
 yle="color: #000000\;"><strong>Rubric:</strong> You will earn up to 6 poin
 ts for the content and requirements of your initial post (each paragraph: 
 event\, principle\, application) and 4 points for your thoughtful summary 
 and response to the group discussion. To see the complete rubric\, click o
 n the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click "Show Ru
 bric."</span></p>\n<p class="kl_module_progress_completion" style="display
 : none\; color: #030303\;">Module Item Completion (built in browser\, hidd
 en in app)</p><script src="https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/ac
 count_74070000000000001/attachments/8409019/dp_app.js"></script>
