  Ulisses Soares" href="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/bio
 graphy-ulisses-soares" target="_blank" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.inst
 ructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044/pages/biography-ulisses-soares" data-api-
 returntype="Page">Elder Ulisses Soares’ biography</a></p>\n<p><a title="
 Biography: M. Russell Ballard" href="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/3
 5044/pages/biography-patrick-kearon" target="_blank" data-api-endpoint="ht
 tps://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044/pages/biography-patrick-kea
 ron" data-api-returntype="Page">Elder Patrick Kearon’s biography</a></p>
 \n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>As a reminder\, you can check which apostle y
 ou signed up for here:</p>\n</div>\n<p><span style="color: #df0000\; backg
 round-color: #ffffff\;"><em>[Make a link to your Google Doc here--see Inst
 ructor Setup Notes]--then delete this]</em></span>Signup Sheet Link<span s
 tyle="color: #df0000\; background-color: #ffffff\;"><em>[End Link]</em></s
 pan>)</p>\n<div class="kl_locked">\n<p><span>Where possible\, these should
  be six of the apostle’s most recent general conference talks\, includin
 g (if you choose) talks given in priesthood or women’s sessions. Also\, 
 where possible\, these should be talks given after their call to the apost
 leship. If six are not available\, you may include talks from devotionals 
 or other settings in which the apostle has given talks prior to their call
  as an apostle.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<l
 i>\n<span>The paper should be 2–3 pages long\, with a word count between
  750 and 1\,000 words. State the word count below your conclusion. The bib
 liography\, a title page\, or any other addenda will </span><i><span>not <
 /span></i><span>count toward the word count. </span>\n</li>\n<li><span>Sub
 mit the paper as a Word document or PDF in 12-point Times New Roman font\,
  double spaced\, with one-inch margins.</span></li>\n<li><span>Use the rub
 ric below as a checklist to see if you meet all the requirements. See the 
 <a title="Apostle Research Paper: Introduction" href="https://byu.instruct
 ure.com/courses/35044/pages/apostle-research-paper-introduction" data-api-
 endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044/pages/apostle-r
 esearch-paper-introduction" data-api-returntype="Page">assignment descript
 ion</a> for more details. You may also review <a href="https://drive.googl
 e.com/file/d/1GvobGQCqXo_3Kri3eWqDgTuZxiieVHql/view?usp=sharing">this exam
 ple paper</a> to help you.</span></li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n<p class="kl_module
 _progress_completion" style="display: none\;">Module Item Completion (buil
 t in browser\, hidden in app)</p><script src="https://instructure-uploads.
 s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409019/dp_app.js">
 </script>
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discussion: Preparing for General Conference [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTSTAMP:20260926T060000Z
UID:event-assignment-1441112
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/files/13505106/d
 ownload?hidden=1)\n\nEstimated time: 30 minutes\n\nAfter you have read the
  assigned readings\, share any thoughts you have about these two questions
 :\n\n*\n\nHow can you prepare to get the most out of general conference? H
 ow can you set the stage to gain what you need or hope for? Highlight a fe
 w specific goals that have come to mind as you’ve studied this unit. You
  may also have some of your own traditions you can share. \n\n(As you rea
 d others’ posts\, keep in mind that sharing these ideas is not meant to 
 be a comprehensive checklist to overwhelm you\; simply consider how to imp
 lement and adapt any ideas that seem inspiring and reasonable to you.)\n\n
 *\n\nHow should you respond when teachings are hard? Once when Jesus Chris
 t was teaching in a synagogue\, “many therefore of his disciples\, when 
 they had heard [his teachings]\, said\, This is an hard saying\; who can h
 ear it?” (John 6:60). Sometimes the counsel we hear at general conferenc
 e can be difficult. Maybe we feel rebuked\; maybe the delivery of a teachi
 ng feels harsh or insensitive\; or maybe we simply feel some doubt or pers
 onal opposition to something that is taught. What tools or principles have
  you learned in this unit that could maybe be helpful as you receive the 
 messages taught and then later choose how to respond?\n\nWrite a solid par
 agraph (minimum 4 sentences) to answer each question. Then\, reply thought
 fully to two other students' comments\, sharing insights from their respon
 se or otherwise extending the conversation. Your replies can be to other p
 osts and/or to comments on your post.\n\nThis is a small group discussion
 \, so please participate in a timely manner as other students will be awai
 ting your post before they can respond. Your post and replies are due by d
 ate indicated at the top of this discussion. NOTE: In a Fall or Winter sem
 ester\, this due date will be Friday so you can focus on watching conferen
 ce on Saturday.\n\nRubric: You will earn up to 6 points for your original 
 post (3 points per question) and 2 points for each of your response posts.
  To see the complete rubric\, click on the three dots in the top right cor
 ner of this page. Then click "Show Rubric."\n\nModule Item Completion (bui
 lt in browser\, hidden in app)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=10&year=2026#assignment_1441112
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instruct
 ure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409020
 /dp_app.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructure-uploads.s3.a
 mazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8073295/canvas-byuonlin
 e-app.css"><div id="kl_wrapper_3" class="kl_basic_bar kl_wrapper">\n<div i
 d="kl_banner_image"><img class="kl_image_full_width" style="width: 100%\; 
 height: auto\; max-width: 100%\;" src="https://byu.instructure.com/courses
 /35044/files/13505106/download?hidden=1" alt="" width="764" height="177" d
 ata-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35044/files/1
 3505106" data-api-returntype="File" data-decorative="true" loading="lazy">
 </div>\n<div><span style="font-size: 10pt\;"><em>Estimated time: 30 minute
 s</em></span></div>\n<div id="kl_custom_block_0">\n<p>After you have read 
 the assigned readings\, share any thoughts you have about these two questi
 ons:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>How can you prepare to get the most out o
 f general conference?</strong> How can you set the stage to gain what you 
 need or hope for? Highlight a few specific goals that have come to mind as
  you’ve studied this unit. You may also have some of your own traditions
  you can share.&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>(As you read others’ posts\, keep in mind
  that sharing these ideas is not meant to be a comprehensive checklist to 
 overwhelm you\; simply consider how to implement and adapt any ideas that 
 seem inspiring and reasonable to you.)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>How sh
 ould you respond when teachings are hard?</strong> Once when Jesus Christ 
 was teaching in a synagogue\, “many therefore of his disciples\, when th
 ey had heard <span class="clarity-word">[his teachings]\,</span> said\, Th
 is is an hard saying\; who can hear it?” (John 6:60). Sometimes the coun
 sel we hear at general conference can be difficult. Maybe we feel rebuked
 \; maybe the delivery of a teaching feels harsh or insensitive\; or maybe 
 we simply feel some doubt or personal opposition to something that is taug
 ht. What tools or principles have you learned in this unit that could mayb
 e be helpful <em>as you receive</em>&nbsp\;the messages taught and then la
 ter choose how to respond?</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style="color: #3333
 33\;">Write a solid paragraph (minimum 4 sentences) to answer each questio
 n. Then\, reply thoughtfully to two other students' comments\, sharing ins
 ights from their response or otherwise extending the conversation. Your re
 plies can be to other posts and/or to comments on your post.</span></p>\n<
 p><span style="color: #333333\;">This is a small group discussion\, so ple
 ase participate in a timely manner as other students will be awaiting your
  post before they can respond. Your post and replies are due by date indic
 ated at the top of this discussion. <strong>NOTE: In a Fall or Winter seme
 ster\, this due date will be Friday so you can focus on watching conferenc
 e on Saturday</strong>. <br></span></p>\n<p><strong>Rubric:</strong> You w
 ill earn up to 6 points for your original post (3 points per question) and
  2 points for each of your response posts. To see the complete rubric\, cl
 ick on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click "Sh
 ow Rubric."</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p class="kl_module_progress_completion" 
